# QA loop

Run from `front-end/` after any Vue/TypeScript/CSS change. Fix failures before continuing.

```bash
npm run type-check      # vue-tsc --build
npm run format:check    # oxfmt --check src/  (fix with npm run format)
npm run lint            # oxlint + ESLint
npm run test:unit       # Vitest (if the change is covered)
npm run build           # type-check + Vite production build
```

`npm run test:unit` uses Vitest watch by default. For a single run: `npx vitest run`.

Skip tests only for comment-only or docs-only edits (still run type-check + format:check + lint).

## Rules

- Test public behavior (props, DOM, user actions), not Vue internals.
- Do not change observable behavior unless asked.
- Limit the diff to the files the task needs.

## Checklist

- [ ] `npm run type-check` — zero errors
- [ ] `npm run format:check` — clean
- [ ] `npm run lint` — zero warnings
- [ ] `npx vitest run` — pass when tests are affected
- [ ] `npm run build` — succeeds
- [ ] Follows @vue-components.mdc and @vue-components-style.mdc
